-- km_arabic_linguistic · 0121 · the sentence-structure tables, named by the registry
--
-- qr_ss_scope_morph_link holds a word's function, case and sign as they were typed in:
-- Arabic (مبتدا، مضاف اليه), slugs (mudaf_ilayh, rafa_mahall) and English phrases
-- ("naat (Daas, al-Darwish, Ibn Ashur)"). Nothing is shown as typed: each spelling is
-- made a variant of the registry term it means, so a lookup by name lands on the term,
-- and the term's name_ar and badge_color are what a reader sees. Every spelling in the
-- table on 2026-10-02 is here; a new spelling is a new row, never a rule in code.
--
-- The transliterations English prose uses for a term (khabar, maṣdar, iltifāt …) are variants
-- of it too, so the reader is shown the Arabic name where the prose wrote the Latin.
--
-- The case signs had no category: irab_sign is added with its terms (الضمّة … مبنيّ على الفتح).
-- alias_bare follows 0111: Arabic without its ḥarakāt (U+064B–U+0652, U+0670), anything
-- else lower-cased; the worker computes a lookup key the same way.
--
-- Projected to km_quran by scripts/project-gram-terms.mjs (terms and aliases).
--
-- Applied by hand when the ledger is out of step: d1 execute --file, then
--   INSERT OR IGNORE INTO d1_migrations (name) VALUES ('0121_gt_ss_spellings_and_signs.sql');

